{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3285","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3285","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3285\",\"parent_revision\":\"b17b5426f9ec31e57b4ab321aec646816894cd79759f25564dfc63759d0289e4\",\"root_revision\":\"b17b5426f9ec31e57b4ab321aec646816894cd79759f25564dfc63759d0289e4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-29 during a long `/dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268` session. This session's very first system reminder showed only `Contents of /Users/jamienelson/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects)` \u2014 the user's global memory file. The project-level file at `<repo>/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (18K, containing \\\"Pre-Existing Issue Accountability,\\\" the Proactive Fix Gate reference, \\\"Request Progression,\\\" the engineering stance section, and the \\\"can you\\\" = delegate convention) was never shown or referenced anywhere in the session's auto-injected context.\\n\\nConfirmed the file itself is present and readable in this worktree at `.claude/worktrees/crystalline-drifting-fog/.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 this is not a missing-file problem. Read its own header comment: \\\"This is the project's single CLAUDE.md (root CLAUDE.md was removed \u2014 see git history commit 662e0434 for the original move, and the 'chore(beads)' commit that inadvertently recreated it).\\\" Confirmed via `ls`/`find` that no `CLAUDE.md` exists at the repository root in this worktree \u2014 only `AGENTS.md` does, and `.claude/CLAUDE.md` imports it via `@../AGENTS.md`.\\n\\nConsequence, observed directly in-session: instructions that only exist in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` were unavailable, leading to session behavior that didn't follow the project's own standing rules until the user pointed at the specific rule text and it was located by manually reading the file. The most concrete instance: the \\\"Pre-Existing Issue Accountability\\\" rule (report-and-default-to-backlog, no permission gate for filing) was not followed for several session findings because its text was never in context.\\n\\nRoot cause not diagnosed: whether Claude Code's project-memory auto-load only scans repository-root `CLAUDE.md` (and `.claude/CLAUDE.md` was never a supported auto-load location, making the commit-662e0434 move itself the bug) or whether `.claude/CLAUDE.md` should be auto-loaded and something else (a worktree-specific path resolution issue, a session/harness configuration gap) suppressed it is not established here \u2014 this item captures the observed absence and its consequence, not a diagnosed mechanism.\\n\\nUser-provided context: a proposed fix was discussed \u2014 a thin root `CLAUDE.md` containing only `@.claude/CLAUDE.md` (mirroring how `.claude/CLAUDE.md` itself imports `@../AGENTS.md`) \u2014 restoring auto-load without duplicating content. Noted that a prior \\\"chore(beads)\\\" commit already re-created a root CLAUDE.md once and it was reverted, so this needs deliberate handling, not another accidental re-creation. Not yet applied; flagged as a hypothesis for grooming to validate.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 development-harness /dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"75d96a97097dd96776d62ca0bee706851c43f9689a9f76799e7473ddfa5e56f6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSByyg\"}"}